' Observed behavior: current calls use one wrapper; permission policy recognizes only that wrapper.
' Design reason: two disclosure paths share target resolution, validation and remote execution.
' Pending implementation: shared executor wiring includes existing Host permission and confirmation hooks.
' Stable block identity retained for existing document links.

actor Model
participant "Tool pipeline / Host hooks" as Pipeline
participant "Agent adapter / CallTool" as Entry
participant "MateToolExecutor" as Executor
participant "Trusted business bindings" as Bindings
participant "MateToolClient" as Client
participant "Mate" as Mate

alt Agent direct tool
  Model -> Pipeline : business_name(args)
  Pipeline -> Entry : resolve Agent adapter
else Skill business tool
  Model -> Pipeline : CallTool({tool, args})
  Pipeline -> Entry : resolve CallTool
end
Pipeline -> Pipeline : validate registered tool schema
Pipeline -> Bindings : Host resolves scope and permission
Bindings --> Pipeline : permission decision or error
Pipeline -> Pipeline : existing permission / confirmation once
alt allowed
  Pipeline -> Entry : execute
  Entry -> Executor : business name, args, allowed scope
  Executor -> Bindings : resolve trusted target and schema
  Bindings --> Executor : ID and business schema or error
  Executor -> Executor : validate business args before HTTP
  opt target and args are valid
  Executor -> Client : callTool(ID, args, execution credentials)
  Client -> Mate : one execute request
  Mate --> Client : authority checks and result
  Client --> Executor : result or error
  end
  Executor --> Entry : normalized result or validation error
  Entry --> Pipeline : tool result
else denied / cancelled / invalid outer schema
  Pipeline -> Pipeline : fail without remote execution
end
Pipeline --> Model : ToolResultMessage
note over Entry,Bindings
  Adapters use direct Agent bindings.
  CallTool uses direct Skill bindings.
  Framework tools and model-provided IDs are not valid targets.
end note
note over Client,Mate
  Forward only the headers provided by the Host.
  Never replay execute after timeout, disconnect or Mate error.
  Metadata queries do not carry execution credentials.
end note
